      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T14:40:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we already have other manager classes that take dependencies objects in their constructors?\n\nI\u0027m not sure this is a good idea since typically manager classes are returned by SystemServiceRegistry, which caches the service that is fetched. Additionally sInstance also caches the first ConnectivityManager that is created in a given classloader. If these caches are be populated with a ConnectivityManager that has the incorrect dependencies, then other ConnectivityManagers that are created later will have the same incorrect dependencies.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 950,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 950,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "e51bedb56fc0073f8d07e3837cc79c54c7e2a245",
