        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-06T08:29:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is discussed in here:\nhttps://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/2732634/comment/2a98f444_1a850874/\n\nWhere we want this method to be easier to deprecate, given that once bpf maps have all information needed, the method could be replaced by something like\nint isUidNetworkingBlocked(int uid, int networkId)\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "2fc86172_a97ad988",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6198,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 6198,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "e51bedb56fc0073f8d07e3837cc79c54c7e2a245",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b542975_348546f7",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 6198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-06T08:57:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it might be quite a while (potentially years) until BPF maps know enough about networks that this will be possible.\n\nAlso, I don\u0027t see how changing the method makes it easier to deprecate. It\u0027s definitely possible to have both methods be called the same, since the parameters are different.\n\nBTW, can this API take the same parameters as NetworkPolicyManager#isUidNetworkingBlocked? If not, then how will the caller know what to pass in for isDataSaverEnabled?",
      "parentUuid": "f486c090_0445d220",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6198,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 6198,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "e51bedb56fc0073f8d07e3837cc79c54c7e2a245",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4b23ef5a_fd9f3078",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 6198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-06T12:17:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Done. But immediately added back at aosp/2742874 , given that this CL is big already.\n\n2. This API cannot take the same parameters as NetworkPolicyManager#isUidNetworkingBlocked.\nBecause NPMS is the source of data saver switch on/off status.\nIt changes mUidState accordingly when it changes.\nSo NetworkPolicyManager#isUidNetworkingBlocked does not need such input from parameter.\nBut we don\u0027t have such information in bpf, so we can only know that from input.\nWe can learn that from ACTION_RESTRICT_BACKGROUND_CHANGED like Tethering did: https://osscs.corp.google.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java;l\u003d1191?q\u003dACTION_RESTRICT_BACKGROUND_CHANGED\u0026ss\u003dandroid\n\nAnd call this api with that input.\n\nSee if it works for you.",
      "parentUuid": "2b542975_348546f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6198,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 6198,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "e51bedb56fc0073f8d07e3837cc79c54c7e2a245",
